# 1. Status model

Every defect uses four independent status axes. Do not collapse them into one word.

## 1.1 Implementation status

- `NOT_STARTED`
- `IN_PROGRESS`
- `CANDIDATE_COMPLETE`
- `REMEDIATION_REQUIRED`
- `BLOCKED_BY_DEPENDENCY`
- `BLOCKED_BY_EVIDENCE`
- `BLOCKED_BY_PRODUCT_DECISION`
- `NO_CHANGE_REQUIRED_CURRENT_HEAD`
- `NOT_APPLICABLE_CURRENT_HEAD`
- `DEFERRED`

`CANDIDATE_COMPLETE` means implementation and local/self verification are complete enough for independent review. It does **not** mean CLEAN.

`BLOCKED_BY_DEPENDENCY` means the defect may be understood and queued, but implementation is not permitted until the named semantic/review dependency is satisfied. `BLOCKED_BY_EVIDENCE` means implementation would be speculative because the causal evidence required to choose a correction is not yet sufficient.

`NO_CHANGE_REQUIRED_CURRENT_HEAD` means a fresh implementation-side current-source revalidation found that intervening code already satisfies the planned invariant, so no new semantic implementation commit is presently required. This is **not** an independent CLEAN verdict. The runner records the exact source/evidence basis and immediately continues to other actionable work while the defect remains eligible for independent review/closure.

`NOT_APPLICABLE_CURRENT_HEAD` means the historical path or architecture described by the defect no longer exists in current source and no equivalent reachable path was found during fresh implementation-side revalidation. This is **not** an independent CLEAN verdict. Record why the historical contract is no longer applicable, then continue to other actionable work.

## 1.2 Self-review status

- `PENDING`
- `PASS_NO_KNOWN_BLOCKERS`
- `FOUND_BLOCKER`
- `NOT_PERFORMED`

An implementation model may self-review its own commit, but self-review never establishes independent closure.

## 1.3 Independent-review status

- `PENDING`
- `NOT_CLEAN`
- `CLEAN`
- `CLEAN_WITH_WAIVERS`

Only this axis controls correctness closure.

## 1.4 Closure-record status

- `OPEN`
- `CLOSED`

Closure is metadata/evidence sealing after independent review. A closure commit may not create a new semantic decision.

---

# 2. Non-negotiable remediation protocol

## 2.1 Fresh-source and pinned-plan rule

At the beginning of each implementation run, before choosing any defect:

1. fresh-fetch `plan/remediation`;
2. resolve the exact remote Plan SHA;
3. read the complete Master Plan by concatenating every file under `remediation/master-plan/parts/` in lexical filename order at that exact Plan SHA;
4. record the Plan SHA in the run/handoff record;
5. keep that exact Plan SHA pinned for the duration of the run unless the user explicitly instructs adoption of a newer plan or the pinned plan itself defines a controlled migration rule.

Do not check out `plan/remediation` into the implementation working tree merely to read the plan. Read it from the fetched remote ref or exact commit so the implementation branch remains unchanged. A later commit on `plan/remediation` does not silently replace the pinned governing plan mid-run.

Read **all** plan parts from the same pinned Plan SHA. Never mix parts from different Plan SHAs, never treat one part as the whole plan, and verify the manifest-provided whole-plan SHA-256 when available before execution.

Before each correction:

1. fresh-fetch `checkpoint/pre-baseline-review`;
2. fresh-fetch `review/remediation`;
3. fresh-fetch `ledger/remediation`;
4. identify the exact current implementation HEAD and parent plus the current review/ledger heads;
5. inspect whether a new independent review targets a candidate that still requires remediation;
6. inspect the current production source relevant to the selected defect;
7. treat this plan's root-cause text as a hypothesis/checklist where source may have changed;
8. do not implement from an old diff alone.

Fresh current production source is authoritative for **source-state facts**. The pinned Master Plan is authoritative for **workflow, gates, invariants, review discipline, branch authority, and execution policy**. If a source-state hypothesis in the plan conflicts with fresh source, record the discrepancy and follow fresh source without silently changing the pinned governance rules.

